diff --git a/CAPABILITIES.md b/CAPABILITIES.md
index ea1bd3c..3c324ec 100644
--- a/CAPABILITIES.md
+++ b/CAPABILITIES.md
@@ -110,3 +110,9 @@ Stored grants, fixtures, and the dashboard depend on the vocabulary. Adding, rem
 4. Update this document.
 
 **Never rename a capability in place.** Stored grants and every consumer keep the old string, and the result authorizes the wrong thing without an error. Add the new capability, migrate grants to it, then retire the old one.
+
+## Internal Runway pilot
+
+Runner Pool and Runner Lease reads require team-wide `server:view`. Pool configuration is operator-only. The assigned `controller_user` must have team-wide `server:view`, `server:create`, and `server:terminate` to use the fenced controller RPCs. These existing capabilities are reused for the bounded internal pilot; no new capability strings or fixture grants are introduced. An API key does not bypass Team authorization. Direct customer writes to lifecycle records are denied.
+
+Each pool admits at most its configured concurrency, with an additional fixed pilot limit of four active or cleanup-pending leases per Team. A lease remains capacity-consuming until both the VM is absent and GitHub runner cleanup is reported. This is admission accounting, not billing enforcement.
